    "summary": "<p><strong><a href=\"https://openai.com/index/navier-stokes-solution/\">On the Navier–Stokes Millennium Prize Problem</a></strong></p> Impressive result from OpenAI, who used an unreleased model to produce a resolution to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Navier–Stokes_existence_and_smoothness\">the Navier–Stokes existence and smoothness problem</a>, one of the seven <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millennium_Prize_Problems\">Millennium Prize Problems</a> that have been subject to a $1,000,000 prize since May 24th, 2000.</p> <p>The discovery is somewhat overshadowed by accusations of skulduggery from Tristan Buckmaster, an NYU mathematics professor who was collaborating on related problems with Levent Alpöge, an accomplished mathematician who currently works for Anthropic.</p> <...",
